    "lawCode": "Amd §7-118, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1590\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to requiring the posting\nof sample ballots on a board of elections website\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill requires the board of election to post a copy of a sample\nballot, including electronically for use with a computer screen-reading\nprogram, on its website prior to each election as soon as the relevant\ninformation becomes available.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 7-118 of the election law, as amended by\nchapter 157 of the laws of 1996.\n\nSection two sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAt times, election days can be hectic and confusing. Requiring a board\nof elections to post sample ballots, which it already is required to\ncreate, will expedite the voting process. Making this information avail-\nable on the a board of elections website, so that voters can see the\nlayout and options ahead of time, will provide valuable information and\ncan reduce waiting time at the polls.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2015-16: A.600 - Referred to Election Law; S.6522 - Referred to\nElections\n2013-14: A.996 - Referred to Election Law\n2011-12: A.10769 - Referred to Election Law\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nUndetermined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill shall take effect January 1 2019.\n",
